  "articleBody": "Finishing your garage turns unfinished space into a clean, durable extension of your home, but success comes down to solid planning. Overview: A proper finish protects framing, controls drafts, and gives you usable storage. Key Benefits: You gain comfortable utility space, better impact resistance, and improved fire separation between the garage and living areas. Process Breakdown: Work begins by inspecting for moisture or leaks, planning out lighting, storage framing, and outlets, adding proper insulation, hanging and finishing drywall, and sealing all penetrations. Real Examples: A homeowner in Littleton needed built-in storage framing and fire-rated drywall on a shared wall, requiring careful trade coordination for safety. What to Prepare Before You Start: Check whether your garage shares walls or ceilings with living spaces, note any past water leaks on the concrete, and check local permit requirements before altering electrical or insulation. When you are ready to get started, Abraham Becerra and the team at HH Remodeling LLC can handle your framing, drywall, and finish carpentry needs from start to finish. Reach out at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}